<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.2.4: Properties of Exponents with Rationals</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01252</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.2.4: Properties of Exponents with Rationals</md:title>
    <md:uuid>f029c2d3-2fd3-4ec5-a8e8-4aa4a90a3efe</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down (5 minutes)</title>
<title>Student Activity</title>
<para>The activities you learned in a prior lesson taught you the properties of exponents. These same properties work with rational exponents.</para>
<para>Simplify each, and then check your answers:</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item> \({(x^2)}^\frac13\) 
    <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x^\frac23\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item> \(x^\frac23\;\cdot\;x^\frac23\) 
    <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x^\frac43\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item> \({(x^{-3})}^\frac25\) 
    <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x^{-\frac65}\;=\;\frac1{x^{\displaystyle^\frac65}}\)
  </item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item> \({(x^\frac13)}^{-1}\) 
    <emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(x^{-\frac13}\;=\;\frac1{x^{\displaystyle^\frac13}}\)
  </item>
</list></section>
</content>
</document>
